                <pb facs="0102" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v10/pg76"/>

                <head>No. 33<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On June 27 the Department of State released to the press a statement by Secretary
                    Acheson in which he expressed regret at the steps being taken by Iran which
                    threatened to close down the Abadan refinery. Acheson stated that he was
                    disappointed that the British proposal presented by Jackson had been summarily
                    rejected without study and expressed his hope that Iran would reconsider and
                    seek some formula that would avoid the dangers inherent in its actions and
                    permit the continued operation of the oil industry. <pb facs="0103" n="77"
                        xml:id="pg77"/> For text of Secretary Acheson’s statement, see Department of
                    State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, July 9, 1951, pages 72–73.</p>
            </div>
